{"strongs": "H1143", "word": "בַּ֫יִן", "translit": "be.na.yim", "root": "בין", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "substantive", "gloss": "interval, space between", "definition": "[ בַּ֫יִן ] substantive properly interval, space between ( id. ) — construct בֵּין once Isa 44:4 ( Baer ) בֵּן , בֵּינִי , ֵבּינְךָ , בֵינֵךְ , בֵּינוֺ ( בֵּינָיו Josh 3:4 ; Josh 8:11 Qr ); with plural suffix in plural form בֵּינֵינוּ ( בֵּנֵינוּ ), etc.; also בֵּינוֺת Ezek 10:2 (twice in verse); Ezek 10:6 (twice in verse); Ezek 10:7 (twice in verse) (+ Ezek 1:13 ᵐ5 Hi Ew etc. for דְּמוּת ), בֵּינוֺתֵינוּ Gen 26:28 ; Josh 22:34 ; Judg 11:10 , בֵּינוֺתָם Gen 42:23 ; 2Sam 21:7 ; Jer 25:16 dual בֵּנַיִם (see below); — 1. always (except dual) as preposition in the interval of , between (so Aramaic בֵּין , & plural בֵּינֵי , , ; ), as Gen 15:17 בֵּין הַגְּזָרִים between the pieces, Exod 13:9 and elsewhere בֵּין עֵינֶיךָ between thy eyes (see עַיִן ), Isa 22:11 and elsewhere between the two walls (see חוֺמָה ), Job 24:11 ; Job 30:7 ; Job 40:30 part him between merchants; rather more generally among Hos 13:15 ; Song 2:2 ; Song 2:3 ; Ezek 19:2 ; Ezek 31:3 ; Job 34:37 less exactly within Prov 26:13 a lion is בֵּין הָֽרְחֹבוֺת within the board places (compare Prov 23:13 בְּתוֺךְ ): once with a singular (unusual) Dan 8:16 בֵּין אוּלַי between the Ulai, i.e. between its banks. When the space separating two distinct objects is to be indicated, this is done \\ \\ a. most commonly by repeating בין , as Gen 13:3 בֵּין בֵּיתְאֵל וּבֵין הָעָ֑י literally in the interval of Bethel, and in the interval of `Ai, i.e. between Bethel and `Ai, Gen 16:14 ; Gen 17:7 ; Gen 31:50 ; Gen 31:51 + often \\ \\ b. more rarely by בֵּין ֗֗֗ לְ , Gen 1:6 dividing בֵּין מַיִם לָמָ֑יִם literally in the interval of waters with reference to waters, i.e. between the waters and the waters, Lev 20:25 ; Lev 27:33 ; Deut 17:8 (3 t. in verse); 2Sam 19:36 ; 1Kgs 3:9 ; Ezek 41:18 ; Ezek 42:20 ; Ezek 44:23 (twice in verse); Jonah 4:11 ; Mal 3:18 (twice in verse); 2Chr 14:10 . \\ \\ c. by בֵּין ֗֗֗ וּלְ Joel 2:17 . \\ \\ d. by בֵּין ֗֗֗ לְבֵין Isa 59:2 . בֵּין is used not only of actual locality, but also with verbs of dividing (figurative) Gen 1:14 ; Lev 10:10 , and of judging, knowing, teaching, etc., if the idea of distinguishing be involved, as Gen 16:5 ; 2Sam 19:36 הַאֵדַע בֵּין טוֺב לְרָע can I discern between good and evil ? 1Kgs 3:9 ; Jonah 4:11 ; Gen 31:49 (watch between ), Judg 11:10 (hear), Josh 22:27 (witness), Isa 2:4 and he shall judge (arbitrate) between the nations, Isa 5:3 ; Lev 27:33 ; Ezek 44:23 ; Mal 3:18 ; 2Chr 14:10 (see RV ); and in other metaphoric applications, as of a covenant or sign between two contracting parties, Gen 9:12 ; Gen 9:15 ; Exod 31:13 +; or an oath Gen 26:28 ; 2Sam 21:7 enmity or strife Gen 3:15 ; Gen 13:7 ; Deut 25:1 ; Prov 6:19 peace 1Kgs 5:26 good-will Prov 14:9 . — It is used of time in the phrase of P בֵּין הָעַרְבַּיִם (see below עֶרֶב ), & Neh 5:18 בֵּין עֲשֶׂרֶת יָמִים during the interval of ten days, i.e. every ten days (unusual).With other prepositions: — \\ \\ a. אֶלבֵּֿין , after a verb implying motion, in between, in among Ezek 31:10 ; Ezek 31:14 . So אֶלבֵּֿינוֺת לְ ib. Ezek 10:2 . \\ \\ b. בְּבֵן Isa 44:4 in the midst of, amongst ( ᵐ5 Ew Di Che כְּבֵין מַיִם חָצִיר ). \\ \\ c. עַלבֵּֿין nearly as אֶלבֵּֿין Ezek 19:11 \\ \\ d. מִבֵּין from between: Gen 49:10 nor the ruler's staff מִבֵּין רַגְלָיו from between his feet (where, as the king sits in state, he holds it), Exod 25:22 from between the cherubim (so Num 7:89 ), Hos 2:4 ; Zech 6:1 ; Zech 9:7 ; Deut 28:57 the after-birth הַיּוֺצֵת מִבֵּין רַגְלֶיהָ that cometh forth from between her feet, i.e. from her womb (compare Il. 19. 10 πεσεῖν μετὰ ποσσὶ γυναικός ) Repeated 2Kgs 16:14 to specify the two objects from between which a thing is moved. Ezek 47:18 is difficult and uncertain: see Commentaries Less precisely from, the midst of: Num 17:2 מִבֵּין הַשְּׂרֵפָה out of the midst of the burning, Ps 104:12 מִבֵּין עֳפָאִים from amongst the branches they utter their song, Jer 48:45 and a flame מִבֵּין סִיחוֺן from the midst of Sihon (Sihon representing his people: but expression is singular; read perhaps ׳ מִבֵּית ס , compare Num 21:28 ׳ מִקִּרְיַת ס : || in both passages מֵחֶשְׁבּוֺן ), Ezek 37:21 . \\ \\ e. מִבֵּינוֺת לְ from between Ezek 10:2 ; Ezek 10:6 (twice in verse); Ezek 10:7 . 2. Dual בֵּנַ֫יִם space between two armies (= Greek μεταίχμιον ), 1Sam 17:4 ; 1Sam 17:23 אִישׁ הַבֵּנַיִם man of the μεταίχμιον , i.e. champion (of Goliath).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1037')\">BDB1037</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H996')\">H996</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H1143')\">H1143</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1036')\">BDB1036</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1038')\">BDB1038</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>בַּ֫יִן</bdbheb>] <b>substantive</b> properly <highlightword>interval, space between</highlightword> (<placeholder575/> <highlight>id.</highlight>) — construct <bdbheb>בֵּין</bdbheb> once <ref ref=\"Isa 44:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,4)\">Isa 44:4</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Baer')\">Baer</lookup>) <bdbheb>בֵּן</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>בֵּינִי</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>ֵבּינְךָ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>בֵינֵךְ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>בֵּינוֺ</bdbheb> (<bdbheb>בֵּינָיו</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 3:4\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(6,3,4)\">Josh 3:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 8:11\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(6,8,11)\">Josh 8:11</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Qr')\"><reflink>Qr</reflink></lookup>); with plural suffix in plural form <bdbheb>בֵּינֵינוּ</bdbheb> (<bdbheb>בֵּנֵינוּ</bdbheb>), etc.; also <bdbheb>בֵּינוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,2)\">Ezek 10:2</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:6\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,6)\">Ezek 10:6</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:7\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,7)\">Ezek 10:7</ref> (twice in verse) (+ <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:13\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,13)\">Ezek 1:13</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hi')\">Hi</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> etc. for <bdbheb>דְּמוּת</bdbheb>), <bdbheb>בֵּינוֺתֵינוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 26:28\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(1,26,28)\">Gen 26:28</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 22:34\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(6,22,34)\">Josh 22:34</ref>; <ref ref=\"Judg 11:10\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(7,11,10)\">Judg 11:10</ref>, <bdbheb>בֵּינוֺתָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 42:23\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"42\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"42\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(1,42,23)\">Gen 42:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 21:7\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(10,21,7)\">2Sam 21:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 25:16\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(24,25,16)\">Jer 25:16</ref> dual <bdbheb>בֵּנַיִם</bdbheb> (see below); — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> always (except dual) as <b>preposition</b> <highlightword>in the interval of</highlightword>, between (so Aramaic <bdbarc>בֵּין</bdbarc>, &amp; plural <bdbheb>בֵּינֵי</bdbheb>, <placeholder576/>, <placeholder577/>; <placeholder578/>), as <ref ref=\"Gen 15:17\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(1,15,17)\">Gen 15:17</ref> <bdbheb>בֵּין הַגְּזָרִים</bdbheb> <highlight>between</highlight> the pieces, <ref ref=\"Exod 13:9\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,9)\">Exod 13:9</ref> and elsewhere <bdbheb>בֵּין עֵינֶיךָ</bdbheb> <highlight>between</highlight> thy eyes (see  <bdbheb><reflink>עַיִן</reflink></bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Isa 22:11\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(23,22,11)\">Isa 22:11</ref> and elsewhere <highlight>between</highlight> the two walls (see  <bdbheb><reflink>חוֺמָה</reflink></bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Job 24:11\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(18,24,11)\">Job 24:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 30:7\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(18,30,7)\">Job 30:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 40:30\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(18,40,30)\">Job 40:30</ref> part him <highlight>between</highlight> merchants; rather more generally <highlight>among</highlight> <ref ref=\"Hos 13:15\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(28,13,15)\">Hos 13:15</ref>; <ref ref=\"Song 2:2\" b=\"22\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(22,2,2)\">Song 2:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Song 2:3\" b=\"22\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(22,2,3)\">Song 2:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 19:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,19,2)\">Ezek 19:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 31:3\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(26,31,3)\">Ezek 31:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 34:37\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"37\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"37\" onclick=\"bcv(18,34,37)\">Job 34:37</ref> less exactly <highlight>within</highlight> <ref ref=\"Prov 26:13\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(20,26,13)\">Prov 26:13</ref> a lion is <bdbheb>בֵּין הָֽרְחֹבוֺת</bdbheb> <highlight>within</highlight> the board places (compare <ref ref=\"Prov 23:13\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(20,23,13)\">Prov 23:13</ref> <bdbheb>בְּתוֺךְ</bdbheb>): once with a singular (unusual) <ref ref=\"Dan 8:16\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(27,8,16)\">Dan 8:16</ref> <bdbheb>בֵּין</bdbheb> <bdbheb>אוּלַי</bdbheb> <highlight>between</highlight> the Ulai, i.e. between its banks. When the space separating two distinct objects is to be indicated, this is done <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> most commonly by repeating <bdbheb>בין</bdbheb>, as <ref ref=\"Gen 13:3\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(1,13,3)\">Gen 13:3</ref> <bdbheb>בֵּין בֵּיתְאֵל</bdbheb> <bdbheb>וּבֵין הָעָ֑י</bdbheb> literally <highlight>in the interval of</highlight> Bethel, and <highlight>in the interval of</highlight> `Ai, i.e. <highlight>between</highlight> Bethel <highlight>and</highlight> `Ai, <ref ref=\"Gen 16:14\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(1,16,14)\">Gen 16:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 17:7\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(1,17,7)\">Gen 17:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 31:50\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"50\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"50\" onclick=\"bcv(1,31,50)\">Gen 31:50</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 31:51\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"51\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"51\" onclick=\"bcv(1,31,51)\">Gen 31:51</ref> + often <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> more rarely by <bdbheb>בֵּין ֗֗֗ </bdbheb> <bdbheb>לְ</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Gen 1:6\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(1,1,6)\">Gen 1:6</ref> dividing <bdbheb>בֵּין מַיִם לָמָ֑יִם</bdbheb> literally <highlight>in the interval of</highlight> waters <highlight>with reference to</highlight> waters, i.e. <highlight>between</highlight> the waters <highlight>and</highlight> the waters, <ref ref=\"Lev 20:25\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(3,20,25)\">Lev 20:25</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 27:33\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"33\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"33\" onclick=\"bcv(3,27,33)\">Lev 27:33</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 17:8\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(5,17,8)\">Deut 17:8</ref> (3 t. in verse); <ref ref=\"2Sam 19:36\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(10,19,36)\">2Sam 19:36</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 3:9\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(11,3,9)\">1Kgs 3:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 41:18\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(26,41,18)\">Ezek 41:18</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 42:20\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"42\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"42\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(26,42,20)\">Ezek 42:20</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 44:23\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(26,44,23)\">Ezek 44:23</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Jonah 4:11\" b=\"32\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(32,4,11)\">Jonah 4:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Mal 3:18\" b=\"39\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(39,3,18)\">Mal 3:18</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"2Chr 14:10\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(14,14,10)\">2Chr 14:10</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> by <bdbheb>בֵּין ֗֗֗ וּלְ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Joel 2:17\" b=\"29\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(29,2,17)\">Joel 2:17</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>d.</b> by <bdbheb>בֵּין ֗֗֗ לְבֵין</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 59:2\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"59\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"59\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(23,59,2)\">Isa 59:2</ref>. <bdbheb>בֵּין</bdbheb> is used not only of actual locality, but also with verbs of dividing (figurative) <ref ref=\"Gen 1:14\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(1,1,14)\">Gen 1:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 10:10\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(3,10,10)\">Lev 10:10</ref>, and of judging, knowing, teaching, etc., if the idea of <highlight>distinguishing</highlight> be involved, as <ref ref=\"Gen 16:5\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(1,16,5)\">Gen 16:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 19:36\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(10,19,36)\">2Sam 19:36</ref> <bdbheb>הַאֵדַע בֵּין</bdbheb> <bdbheb>טוֺב לְרָע</bdbheb> can I discern <highlight>between</highlight> good and evil ? <ref ref=\"1Kgs 3:9\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(11,3,9)\">1Kgs 3:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jonah 4:11\" b=\"32\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(32,4,11)\">Jonah 4:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 31:49\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"49\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"49\" onclick=\"bcv(1,31,49)\">Gen 31:49</ref> (watch <highlight>between</highlight>), <ref ref=\"Judg 11:10\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(7,11,10)\">Judg 11:10</ref> (hear), <ref ref=\"Josh 22:27\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(6,22,27)\">Josh 22:27</ref> (witness), <ref ref=\"Isa 2:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,2,4)\">Isa 2:4</ref> and he shall judge (arbitrate) <highlight>between</highlight> the nations, <ref ref=\"Isa 5:3\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(23,5,3)\">Isa 5:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 27:33\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"33\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"33\" onclick=\"bcv(3,27,33)\">Lev 27:33</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 44:23\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(26,44,23)\">Ezek 44:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"Mal 3:18\" b=\"39\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(39,3,18)\">Mal 3:18</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 14:10\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(14,14,10)\">2Chr 14:10</ref> (see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('RV')\"><reflink>RV</reflink></lookup>); and in other metaphoric applications, as of a covenant or sign <highlight>between</highlight> two contracting parties, <ref ref=\"Gen 9:12\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(1,9,12)\">Gen 9:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 9:15\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(1,9,15)\">Gen 9:15</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 31:13\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(2,31,13)\">Exod 31:13</ref> +; or an oath <ref ref=\"Gen 26:28\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(1,26,28)\">Gen 26:28</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 21:7\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(10,21,7)\">2Sam 21:7</ref> enmity or strife <ref ref=\"Gen 3:15\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(1,3,15)\">Gen 3:15</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 13:7\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(1,13,7)\">Gen 13:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 25:1\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(5,25,1)\">Deut 25:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 6:19\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(20,6,19)\">Prov 6:19</ref> peace <ref ref=\"1Kgs 5:26\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(11,5,26)\">1Kgs 5:26</ref> good-will <ref ref=\"Prov 14:9\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(20,14,9)\">Prov 14:9</ref>. — It is used of <highlight>time</highlight> in the phrase of <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup> <bdbheb>בֵּין הָעַרְבַּיִם</bdbheb> (see below <bdbheb>עֶרֶב</bdbheb>), &amp; <ref ref=\"Neh 5:18\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(16,5,18)\">Neh 5:18</ref> <bdbheb>בֵּין עֲשֶׂרֶת יָמִים</bdbheb> <highlight>during the interval of </highlight>ten days, i.e. every ten days (unusual).With other prepositions: — <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> <bdbheb>אֶלבֵּֿין</bdbheb>, after a verb implying motion, <highlight>in between, in among</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ezek 31:10\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(26,31,10)\">Ezek 31:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 31:14\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(26,31,14)\">Ezek 31:14</ref>. So <bdbheb>אֶלבֵּֿינוֺת לְ</bdbheb> ib. <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,2)\">Ezek 10:2</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> <bdbheb>בְּבֵן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 44:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,4)\">Isa 44:4</ref> <highlight>in the midst of, amongst</highlight> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Che')\">Che</lookup> <bdbheb>כְּבֵין מַיִם חָצִיר</bdbheb>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> <bdbheb>עַלבֵּֿין</bdbheb> nearly as <bdbheb>אֶלבֵּֿין</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 19:11\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(26,19,11)\">Ezek 19:11</ref> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>d.</b> <bdbheb>מִבֵּין</bdbheb> <highlight>from between:</highlight> <ref ref=\"Gen 49:10\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"49\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"49\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(1,49,10)\">Gen 49:10</ref> nor the ruler's staff <bdbheb>מִבֵּין רַגְלָיו</bdbheb> <highlight>from between</highlight> his feet (where, as the king sits in state, he holds it), <ref ref=\"Exod 25:22\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(2,25,22)\">Exod 25:22</ref> <highlight>from between</highlight> the cherubim (so <ref ref=\"Num 7:89\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"89\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"89\" onclick=\"bcv(4,7,89)\">Num 7:89</ref>), <ref ref=\"Hos 2:4\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(28,2,4)\">Hos 2:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Zech 6:1\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(38,6,1)\">Zech 6:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Zech 9:7\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(38,9,7)\">Zech 9:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 28:57\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"57\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"57\" onclick=\"bcv(5,28,57)\">Deut 28:57</ref> the after-birth <bdbheb>הַיּוֺצֵת מִבֵּין</bdbheb> <bdbheb>רַגְלֶיהָ</bdbheb> that cometh forth <highlight>from between</highlight> her feet, i.e. from her womb (compare Il. 19. 10 <grk>πεσεῖν μετὰ</grk> <grk>ποσσὶ γυναικός</grk>) Repeated <ref ref=\"2Kgs 16:14\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(12,16,14)\">2Kgs 16:14</ref> to specify the two objects <highlight>from between</highlight> which a thing is moved. <ref ref=\"Ezek 47:18\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"47\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"47\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(26,47,18)\">Ezek 47:18</ref> is difficult and uncertain: see Commentaries Less precisely <highlight>from, the midst of:</highlight> <ref ref=\"Num 17:2\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(4,17,2)\">Num 17:2</ref> <bdbheb>מִבֵּין הַשְּׂרֵפָה</bdbheb> <highlight>out of the midst of</highlight> the burning, <ref ref=\"Ps 104:12\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"104\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"104\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(19,104,12)\">Ps 104:12</ref> <bdbheb>מִבֵּין עֳפָאִים</bdbheb> <highlight>from amongst</highlight> the branches they utter their song, <ref ref=\"Jer 48:45\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"45\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"45\" onclick=\"bcv(24,48,45)\">Jer 48:45</ref> and a flame <bdbheb>מִבֵּין סִיחוֺן</bdbheb> <highlight>from the midst of</highlight> Sihon (Sihon representing his people: but expression is singular; read perhaps <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מִבֵּית ס</bdbheb>, compare <ref ref=\"Num 21:28\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(4,21,28)\">Num 21:28</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מִקִּרְיַת ס</bdbheb>: || in both passages <bdbheb>מֵחֶשְׁבּוֺן</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Ezek 37:21\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(26,37,21)\">Ezek 37:21</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>e.</b> <bdbheb>מִבֵּינוֺת</bdbheb> <bdbheb>לְ</bdbheb> <highlight>from between</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,2)\">Ezek 10:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:6\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,6)\">Ezek 10:6</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 10:7\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(26,10,7)\">Ezek 10:7</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> <b>Dual</b> <bdbheb>בֵּנַ֫יִם</bdbheb> space between two armies (= Greek <grk>μεταίχμιον</grk>), <ref ref=\"1Sam 17:4\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(9,17,4)\">1Sam 17:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 17:23\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(9,17,23)\">1Sam 17:23</ref> <bdbheb>אִישׁ הַבֵּנַיִם</bdbheb> <highlight>man of the</highlight> <grk>μεταίχμιον</grk>, i.e. champion (of Goliath). </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Isa 44:4", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 44, "verse": 4}, {"raw": "Josh 3:4", "book": "JOS", "chapter": 3, "verse": 4}, {"raw": "Josh 8:11", "book": "JOS", "chapter": 8, "verse": 11}, {"raw": "Ezek 10:2", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 10, "verse": 2}, {"raw": "Ezek 10:6", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 10, "verse": 6}, {"raw": "Ezek 10:7", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 10, "verse": 7}, {"raw": "Ezek 1:13", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 1, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Gen 26:28", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 26, "verse": 28}, {"raw": "Josh 22:34", "book": "JOS", "chapter": 22, "verse": 34}, {"raw": "Judg 11:10", "book": "JDG", "chapter": 11, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "Gen 42:23", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 42, "verse": 23}, {"raw": "2Sam 21:7", "book": 